00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:12.130
I will fight for you and believe in you

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:18.040
Gather your unparalleled tenderness, yeah, Precure

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:29.990
Being a Mommy's Tough!

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:29.990
Being a Mommy's Tough!

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:38.210
Her heart rate appears to be normal.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.900
Nothing out of the ordinary.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.870
Thank goodness she isn't ill.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.980
Lancece!

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:57.660
Help yourself to some milk.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:04.100
It seems she isn't hungry, either.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.690
So why is she throwing tantrums?

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:12.300
And why did Ai's crying give Ira and Mammo so much Egogy?

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.720
I can't bear to see Ai like this.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:22.480
We've got to get her back to her happy self!

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:25.640
Where am I?

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.080
Peekaboo!

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:30.350
Yo! Checka Racka!

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.540
Ai, let's play!

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:48.450
Go to sleep,

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.470
go to sleep,

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.830
in your mother's arms... {Different translation from what we've had before, but this fits better. Nobody'll notice, right?}

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:02.450
Ai, look, this is fun!

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.050
Come play with us!

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.690
Hello.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.700
Welcome, Ryouko.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.090
I'll have the usual.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.060
Rikka?

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:19.050
Wow, what happened to you girls?

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.540
I've never seen you all so pooped.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.740
We were taking care of Ai...

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:28.980
But she was in a bad mood the whole time,

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.230
and ended up crying herself to sleep.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.120
She was always so happy before today...

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.990
Mom, how do you calm a crying baby?

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.210
It's not easy.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:44.360
There's no surefire way to do it.

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:45.920
Really?

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.740
Sometimes, babies just like to be grumpy.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:49.700
Very true.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.550
But you're a pediatrician, right?

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.810
Don't you know everything about babies?

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.510
It'd be nice if anyone could.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:04.210
Babies can't talk, so they cry to complain.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:07.180
Crying is how babies give you a hint.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.710
A hint?

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:12.760
Speaking of which, Rikka cried a lot as a baby.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:16.300
I never slept on the nights you cried through.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:20.700
I held you while you wailed,

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:23.760
and walked through the city all night long.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.500
My arms hurt and my back was killing me,

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.850
and you still didn't stop crying.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.670
It made me think I was a horrible mother!

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.650
And then I'd start crying along with you.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.280
A horrible mother?

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.330
She was a night-crier, huh?

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.820
She was wailing?

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:48.750
I'd never think someone as diligent as Rikka would have been such a crybaby...

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:53.390
I-I was a baby, come on!

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:56.370
What kind of baby was Mana?

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:01.530
Mana ate, slept, and smiled a lot,

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:04.070
so she wasn't as much of a handful.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.380
But you wouldn't believe the trouble she was when she learned to walk!

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:12.850
If she fell out of bed, she'd roll off to who-knows-where!

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:16.050
If we went for a stroll, she'd walk off on her own!

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:19.620
She'd try to jump from the top of the jungle gym!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.930
And then she let a jarful of crickets she caught loose in the house...

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:25.320
Stop!

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:26.870
Was there more?

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:28.770
Oh, <i>much</i> more.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:31.210
You might not have been a big crier yourself,

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:33.300
but you made your poor mother one.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.220
How fitting for Mana.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.940
Even her toddlerhood was filled with epic adventure!

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.050
diner

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.050
Pig's Tail

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.080
Thanks for the help. {I don't fucking care anymore if it's not possible to split this line properly this show is fucking garbage anyway.}

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:51.450
